<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/007C">Definition <span data-tag="007C">1.5.6.4</span>.</a> Let $f: A \rightarrow B$ be a morphism of simplicial sets. We will say that $f$ is <em>inner anodyne</em> if it belongs to the weakly saturated class of morphisms generated by the collection of all inner horn inclusions $\Lambda ^{n}_{i} \hookrightarrow \Delta ^ n$ (so that $0 &lt; i &lt; n$). </p>
